From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:24:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gsupplicant: offer plain WPA2-PSK on an access point

Since "gsupplicant: Set MFP optional and key_mgmt for PSK" every PSK
network is added with key_mgmt "SAE WPA-PSK WPA-PSK-SHA256" and MFP
optional. That includes the access point the wifi plugin builds for
tethering, so the hotspot advertises WPA3 transition mode and a station
may pick SAE or PSK-SHA256.

Many phone drivers cannot do either in AP mode. MediaTek's gen4m rejects
such an association with status 43 (invalid AKMP), logging
"rsnParserCheckForRSNCCMPPSK: RSN with invalid AKMP", so a FuriPhone
FLX1s could not join a Q25's hotspot at all.

Keep the new default for stations, and give an access point
(G_SUPPLICANT_MODE_MASTER) plain WPA-PSK as before.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gsupplicant/supplicant.c | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gsupplicant/supplicant.c b/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
index 7e0b14f..cc0efb0 100644
--- a/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
+++ b/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
@@ -5184,9 +5184,20 @@ static void add_network_security(DBusMessageIter *dict, GSupplicantSSID *ssid)
 		add_network_security_ciphers(dict, ssid);
 		break;
 	case G_SUPPLICANT_SECURITY_PSK:
-		key_mgmt = "SAE WPA-PSK WPA-PSK-SHA256";
-		ieee80211w = G_SUPPLICANT_MFP_OPTIONAL;
-		add_network_ieee80211w(dict, ssid, ieee80211w);
+		/*
+		 * An access point (tethering) offers plain WPA2-PSK. Offering
+		 * SAE and PSK-SHA256 as well lets stations pick an AKM that
+		 * many phone drivers cannot do in AP mode: MediaTek's gen4m
+		 * rejects such an association with status 43 (invalid AKMP),
+		 * so no client could join the hotspot at all.
+		 */
+		if (ssid->mode == G_SUPPLICANT_MODE_MASTER) {
+			key_mgmt = "WPA-PSK";
+		} else {
+			key_mgmt = "SAE WPA-PSK WPA-PSK-SHA256";
+			ieee80211w = G_SUPPLICANT_MFP_OPTIONAL;
+			add_network_ieee80211w(dict, ssid, ieee80211w);
+		}
 		add_network_security_psk(dict, ssid);
 		add_network_security_ciphers(dict, ssid);
 		add_network_security_proto(dict, ssid);
